  "policy": "A legal hold SUSPENDS all deletion, purge, or anonymization of the named subject's records for the duration of the matter, and OVERRIDES retention-window expiry and routine cleanup. A hold is IN EFFECT on a given date when that date is on or after 'placed' AND before 'expires' (if set) AND before 'released' (if set); 'expires' is a scheduled automatic lapse and 'released' is an early manual release, either of which ends the hold. A subject with any hold IN EFFECT as of the current date MUST NOT have records purged, exported outside authorized handling, or anonymized. Holds that have expired or been released do NOT block deletion. Evaluate in-effect status against the current date.",
